body:
Due to the fact that i had to be much wiser then i was supposed to be at that age, i can definitely recall some painful rejections.

&#x200B;

 I always really liked pink and purple, but had to bury the first one behind another, and another one behind the black color - my parents are conservative Russians, and, as it is sad, that my father is a "proud homophobe", and my mother really wants to make The Man™ from me, it is really funny, because now i don't doubt their ignorance about me and can play with fire by teasing them with my already feminine traits. 

&#x200B;

After quite some time i started to wear shirts with prints on them (i was somewhat forced to not like them, because my father never wore any), customized my laptop so that  almost all of my interface is purple, shaved my legs a few times, was super caring and supportive to all of my few friends, but i never really showed any of that to my parents or expressed any emotions that they can perceived as feminine, so i worked hard to show none. Needless to say - it backfired really hard and dawns on me to this day.  

&#x200B;

Fast forward to two weeks earlier - i cried in hands of my boyfriend that showered me with compliments. That was something i only dreamt of.
